# Create Session

> Create a live session from an image, a Persona, and a voice. Returns session settings, a WebSocket control credential, and RTC media credentials. For a minimal working request, see the [Quickstart](/streaming-avatar/get-started/quickstart).

> **Connection, duration, and errors**
>
> The response includes control and media credentials. See [Sessions](https://docs.vivix.ai/streaming-avatar/api-references/sessions#connect-and-control) to connect, [session management](https://docs.vivix.ai/streaming-avatar/integrate/sessions.md) for automatic closure, and [Errors](https://docs.vivix.ai/streaming-avatar/api-references/sessions#errors) for error codes.


## OpenAPI

````yaml streaming-avatar/api-references/openapi.json POST /v1/realtime-avatar/sessions
openapi: 3.1.0
info:
  title: Vivix Streaming Avatar API
  version: 1.0.0
  description: REST endpoints for Streaming Avatar sessions, voices, and characters.
servers:
  - url: https://api.vivix.ai
security:
  - bearerAuth: []
paths:
  /v1/realtime-avatar/sessions:
    post:
      summary: Create Session
      description: >-
        Create a live session from an image, a Persona, and a voice. Returns
        session settings, a WebSocket control credential, and RTC media
        credentials. For a minimal working request, see the
        [Quickstart](/streaming-avatar/get-started/quickstart).
      operationId: createSession
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              type: object
              properties:
                model:
                  type: string
                  description: Use `vivix-a1-stream`.
                idempotency_key:
                  type: string
                  description: >-
                    Optional key for retrying session creation. Reuse the same
                    key when retrying the same request; use a new key for a new
                    session.
                session:
                  type: object
                  description: >-
                    Opening avatar and source image. Omit this object for a
                    single avatar with one image. Use `session.update` to change
                    the selected avatar or image during the session.
                  properties:
                    mode:
                      type: string
                      description: >-
                        Session mode. Defaults to `video_avatar`, which streams
                        avatar video, speech, and text events.
                      enum:
                        - video_avatar
                      default: video_avatar
                    active_avatar_id:
                      type: string
                      description: >-
                        Initial avatar ID. Omit when supplying one avatar;
                        specify it when supplying multiple avatars.
                    source_image_id:
                      type: string
                      description: >-
                        Opening image ID. Omit to use the active avatar’s
                        default image, or its only image. Set this when no
                        default image can be selected.
                output:
                  type: object
                  description: >-
                    Required video output settings. Set the aspect ratio and
                    resolution when creating the session.
                  properties:
                    aspect_ratio:
                      type: string
                      description: >-
                        Requested avatar video aspect ratio. Supported values
                        are `9:16` and `16:9`. Use a starting image with the
                        same aspect ratio—a mismatched image will noticeably
                        degrade video quality.
                    resolution:
                      type: string
                      description: >-
                        Requested avatar video resolution. Supported values are
                        `480p` and `720p`.
                avatars:
                  type: array
                  description: >-
                    Available characters. Supply at least one, with unique
                    `avatar_id` values. Each avatar selected for video needs a
                    source image. Configure the shared voice in
                    `pipeline_config.tts_config`.
                  items:
                    type: object
                    properties:
                      avatar_id:
                        type: string
                        description: >-
                          Caller-defined avatar identifier, unique within the
                          session.
                      persona:
                        type: string
                        description: >-
                          Describe the character's identity, personality,
                          speaking style, response habits, movement preferences,
                          and listening behavior in plain language or Markdown.
                          Vivix uses this Persona to prepare the character's
                          behavior automatically. See [Write a
                          Persona](/streaming-avatar/character/persona).
                        minLength: 1
                      voice:
                        type: object
                        description: >-
                          Optional per-avatar TTS configuration for multi-avatar
                          sessions that require different voices. Provide
                          `provider`, `provider_voice_id`, and `model`. For the
                          normal session-wide voice path, omit this object and
                          configure `pipeline_config.tts_config`. A session TTS
                          configuration takes precedence over every per-avatar
                          voice.
                        properties:
                          provider:
                            type: string
                            description: >-
                              TTS backend, such as
                              `qwen-audio-3.0-tts-flash_ws`, `elevenlabs`, or
                              `qwen3tts`. Required with `provider_voice_id` and
                              `model`.
                          provider_voice_id:
                            type: string
                            description: >-
                              Provider-side voice or style id. Required with
                              `provider` and `model`.
                          model:
                            type: string
                            description: >-
                              Provider TTS model ID. Required with `provider`
                              and `provider_voice_id`.
                          speed:
                            type: number
                            description: >-
                              Speech speed multiplier. The valid range is `0.7`
                              to `1.2`.
                        required:
                          - provider
                          - provider_voice_id
                          - model
                      visual:
                        type: object
                        description: >-
                          Visual rendering settings. Required when this avatar
                          is used for video rendering.
                        properties:
                          source_images:
                            type: array
                            description: >-
                              Registered source images available for this
                              avatar. Required when image-based avatar video
                              rendering is used.
                            items:
                              type: object
                              description: >-
                                One source image that can be selected for avatar
                                video rendering.
                              properties:
                                source_image_id:
                                  type: string
                                  description: >-
                                    Caller-defined source image identifier,
                                    unique within the avatar.
                                url:
                                  type: string
                                  description: >-
                                    Publicly accessible HTTPS URL of the source
                                    image. Its aspect ratio should match
                                    `output.aspect_ratio` (`9:16` or `16:9`)—a
                                    mismatched image will noticeably degrade
                                    video quality.
                                description:
                                  type: string
                                  description: >-
                                    Optional description of the person, pose,
                                    and scene.
                                media_type:
                                  type: string
                                  description: >-
                                    Image media type, such as `image/png` or
                                    `image/jpeg`.
                                opening:
                                  type: object
                                  description: >-
                                    Optional opening speech or action. Supply
                                    `dialogue`, `action`, or both. It runs when
                                    this image is selected and begins rendering.
                                  properties:
                                    dialogue:
                                      type: string
                                      description: Exact opening words to synthesize.
                                    action:
                                      type: object
                                      properties:
                                        prompt:
                                          type: string
                                          description: >-
                                            Visual motion prompt for the opening
                                            action.
                                        duration_ms:
                                          type: integer
                                          minimum: 1
                                          description: Opening action duration in milliseconds.
                                      required:
                                        - prompt
                                        - duration_ms
                                      description: >-
                                        Opening movement, described by a prompt
                                        and duration.
                                    starting_at:
                                      type: integer
                                      minimum: 0
                                      default: 0
                                      description: >-
                                        Delay in milliseconds before the opening
                                        begins, measured from the first frame
                                        becoming available.
                              required:
                                - source_image_id
                                - media_type
                                - url
                          default_source_image_id:
                            type: string
                            description: >-
                              Default image ID. Omit when the avatar has one
                              source image; otherwise set this or
                              `session.source_image_id`.
                        required:
                          - source_images
                    required:
                      - avatar_id
                      - persona
                  minItems: 1
                pipeline_config:
                  type: object
                  description: >-
                    Session-wide speech recognition, speech synthesis, dialogue
                    model, and audio rendering settings. These settings are
                    fixed at session creation.
                  properties:
                    tag_audio_enabled:
                      type: boolean
                      description: >-
                        Play a short vocal cue such as “mm” or “hmm” before the
                        main answer. Defaults to `false`. Also configure the
                        opening in the Persona’s Speaking Style section; see
                        [Short vocal
                        cues](/streaming-avatar/interaction/acknowledgement).
                    tts_config:
                      type: object
                      properties:
                        tts_voice_id:
                          type: string
                          description: >-
                            Built-in voice ID or Vivix cloned `voice_id`.
                            Required when `tts_config` is supplied.
                        tts_provider:
                          type: string
                          description: >-
                            Speech service. For built-in Qwen Audio voices,
                            defaults to `qwen-audio-3.0-tts-flash_ws`. Omit for
                            Vivix cloned voices; specify for other services.
                        tts_model_id:
                          type: string
                          description: >-
                            Speech model. For built-in Qwen Audio voices,
                            defaults to `qwen-audio-3.0-tts-flash`. Omit for
                            Vivix cloned voices; specify for other services.
                        tts_endpoint:
                          type: string
                          description: >-
                            Custom speech-service endpoint. Omit for built-in
                            and Vivix cloned voices.
                        tts_api_key:
                          type: string
                          description: >-
                            Your speech-service API key, when using your own
                            service credentials. Built-in voices need no
                            separate key.
                        payload:
                          type: object
                          description: >-
                            Additional parameters supported by the selected
                            speech service. See [Speech
                            synthesis](/streaming-avatar/integrate/speech-synthesis).
                      required:
                        - tts_voice_id
                      description: >-
                        Session-wide TTS configuration. It takes precedence over
                        every `avatars[].voice`.
                    asr_config:
                      type: object
                      properties:
                        provider:
                          type: string
                          description: >-
                            Recognition service: `doubao` or `nova-3`. Required
                            when supplying `asr_config`; omit the whole object
                            to use the default.
                        language:
                          type: string
                          description: >-
                            Optional. Examples: `zh-CN` or `en-US` for Doubao;
                            `en` for Nova. Controls recognition language, not
                            the reply language.
                      required:
                        - provider
                      description: >-
                        Advanced override. Omit it to use the platform default,
                        `doubao`. Set `provider` (`doubao` for multilingual, or
                        `nova-3` for English-only) and optional `language`. See
                        [`asr_config`](/streaming-avatar/integrate/speech-recognition).
                    llm_config:
                      type: object
                      properties:
                        llm_backend:
                          type: string
                          description: Optional; only `openai` is supported.
                        llm_base_url:
                          type: string
                          description: >-
                            OpenAI-compatible base URL. Supply with `llm_model`
                            to use a custom dialogue service.
                        llm_model:
                          type: string
                          description: Optional custom model name.
                        llm_api_key:
                          type: string
                          description: >-
                            Your dialogue-service API key, when required by the
                            custom service.
                        llm_temperature:
                          type: number
                          description: >-
                            Optional generation temperature; use the range
                            supported by the model.
                        llm_max_output_tokens:
                          type: integer
                          description: Optional generated-token limit, not a word count.
                        llm_extra_payload:
                          type: string
                          description: >-
                            Optional JSON-encoded object string; do not supply a
                            nested object.
                      description: >-
                        Optional dialogue-model configuration. Set
                        `llm_base_url` and `llm_model` for a custom service, or
                        override only generation parameters. See [Dialogue model
                        configuration](/streaming-avatar/integrate/dialogue-model)
                        for field types and examples.
                    a2a_config:
                      type: object
                      description: >-
                        Render the avatar from audio published by your
                        application. See [Pure rendering
